cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "satellite_routing: simulation of source routing for load balancing in software-defined satellite networks"
authors:
  - family-names: Bergamini
    given-names: Federico
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Fede-Berga/satellite_routing"
keywords:
  - satellite networks
  - LEO constellations
  - software-defined networking
  - source routing
  - load balancing
  - discrete-event simulation
abstract: >-
  Discrete-event simulator of a 66-satellite Iridium-like LEO constellation,
  built with SimPy, ns.py and Skyfield. A ground-side controller computes
  source routes from link lengths and exponentially smoothed queue occupancy,
  refreshed every second, and the simulator compares port forwarding with
  early discarding of packets whose route has become stale.
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "A Simulation Study of Source Routing for Load Balancing in Software-Defined Satellite Networks"
